WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.519
Clear ownership prevents findings from stalling between teams.

00:00:04.519 --> 00:00:09.513
Application owners usually manage code, dependencies, and deployment behavior.

00:00:09.513 --> 00:00:14.032
Platform teams manage nodes, runtimes, and Kubernetes components.

00:00:14.032 --> 00:00:18.551
Security maintains policy, intelligence, prioritization guidance, and oversight.

00:00:18.551 --> 00:00:23.070
Registries and build systems also need named owners.

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:29.967
Patch service-level agreements should reflect risk, exposure, and criticality rather than severity alone.

00:00:29.967 --> 00:00:40.669
Define when the clock starts, what counts as remediation, who verifies closure, and how newly exploited conditions change the target date.

00:00:40.669 --> 00:00:46.139
Exceptions and risk acceptance are documented decisions, not silent delay.

00:00:46.139 --> 00:00:53.512
Record affected assets, residual risk, rationale, compensating controls, approver, owner, expiration, and review trigger.

00:00:53.512 --> 00:00:59.933
An exception should return to the remediation queue when its conditions change.

00:00:59.933 --> 00:01:04.928
Reporting should connect vulnerabilities to deployed environments and owners.

00:01:04.928 --> 00:01:19.435
Useful views include aging critical findings, overdue items, stale images, unpatched base-image descendants, unsupported components, exception age, and the difference between fixed images and workloads still running old digests.

00:01:19.435 --> 00:01:34.419
Metrics should measure effectiveness: time from disclosure to triage, rebuild, deployment, and verified closure; percentage remediated within target; recurrence caused by stale templates; production coverage; and failed or rolled-back updates.

00:01:34.419 --> 00:01:38.937
Raw finding counts can rise when visibility improves.

00:01:38.937 --> 00:01:42.981
Governance turns security debt into visible choices.

00:01:42.981 --> 00:01:54.159
Review trends with engineering and leadership, fund recurring base-image and platform maintenance, remove abandoned artifacts, and improve the process where delays repeat.

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:59.153
The aim is reliable risk reduction, not perfect dashboards.
